226:In  conclusion, we estimated a normative model of dynamic functional connectivities in different brain inherent networks, based on a large MDD cohort. We found that the distributions of FEDN-MDD and controls showed more difference when considering the dynamic characteristics compared to static features in functional connectivities. Our results showed that it was necessary to look at the limitation of the casecontrol  paradigm -which collapses individual  patients  with  different neural signatures and even symptoms into one ' average MDD participant ' ,  and  further  understanding  the  heterogeneous  neuroimaging mechanism of MDD. Normative modeling might provide an excellent tool for understanding the heterogeneity of psychiatric disorders, and can be used as complementary to classical case-control comparisons, and this  study  also  posed  a  warning  for  the  limited  potential  of  the biomarkers in psychiatric disorders.
